\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Note that this definition makes sense for finite sets and the intuition we already have for what the cardinality of a finite set is. If there is a bijection between two finite sets, then they definitely have the same (natural number) size; if there is an injection from #{A} to #{B}, then #{B} definitely has to be at least as big as #{A}.}
